er true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options:\n\n- $P$ is a statement. This statement is *true* because $0.5=\\frac{5}{10},$ so it is a rational number.\n\n- $Q$ is a statement. This statement is *false* because $0.5$ is a rational number.\n\n- $R$ is *not* a statement because it is neither true nor false. Rather, it is an instruction.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P$ and $Q$ only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-599cb91c-0d63-5d51-9b83-794e5c17ff8e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-599cb91c-0d63-5d51-9b83-794e5c17ff8e" :answer-field/id #uuid "599cb91c-0d63-5d51-9b83-794e5c17ff8e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1683e4df-7ac1-56de-93fe-3dc1c97b033d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1683e4df-7ac1-56de-93fe-3dc1c97b033d" "answer-f94e743c-7b96-5495-994f-6c9dca697862" "answer-d1a4ddc1-38ac-5eaa-ada1-0c765f9e51ce" "answer-00c6db1d-5927-5c6a-9a41-4fbc644fc1e4" "answer-d9dfa505-d63e-5fd7-9564-b821a3bed62f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1683e4df-7ac1-56de-93fe-3dc1c97b033d" :answer/id #uuid "1683e4df-7ac1-56de-93fe-3dc1c97b033d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P$ and $Q$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f94e743c-7b96-5495-994f-6c9dca697862" :answer/id #uuid "f94e743c-7b96-5495-994f-6c9dca697862" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d1a4ddc1-38ac-5eaa-ada1-0c765f9e51ce" :answer/id #uuid "d1a4ddc1-38ac-5eaa-ada1-0c765f9e51ce" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q$ and $R$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-00c6db1d-5927-5c6a-9a41-4fbc644fc1e4" :answer/id #uuid "00c6db1d-5927-5c6a-9a41-4fbc644fc1e4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9dfa505-d63e-5fd7-9564-b821a3bed62f" :answer/id #uuid "d9dfa505-d63e-5fd7-9564-b821a3bed62f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$R$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ae9ba4f6-2cb2-5711-bd11-5c1b1d70436a" :question/id #uuid "ae9ba4f6-2cb2-5711-bd11-5c1b1d70436a" :question/math-academy-id "q-102847" :question/problem "Which of the following is a mathematical statement?" :question/worked-solution "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false. \n\nOf the given sentences, the only sentence that is either true or false is \"A rectangle has four angles.\" (This sentence is true.)\n\nAll the other sentences are neither true nor false." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a9bbce88-e20f-53a3-b5e8-17d8d8b20865"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a9bbce88-e20f-53a3-b5e8-17d8d8b20865" :answer-field/id #uuid "a9bbce88-e20f-53a3-b5e8-17d8d8b20865" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-27e7f1a2-0340-57ea-a3ec-6b7f16d5e4b4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-27e7f1a2-0340-57ea-a3ec-6b7f16d5e4b4" "answer-ee24fb1c-29c7-5fc5-9eae-4512b626a3d7" "answer-6b7642cc-29be-5f1a-9a16-ef318c444413" "answer-b67f3de7-0824-5db8-a89a-109dbb1c1bc7" "answer-2a6a5fdc-fdac-5d72-9181-7f0590bf65a9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-27e7f1a2-0340-57ea-a3ec-6b7f16d5e4b4" :answer/id #uuid "27e7f1a2-0340-57ea-a3ec-6b7f16d5e4b4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A rectangle has four angles." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee24fb1c-29c7-5fc5-9eae-4512b626a3d7" :answer/id #uuid "ee24fb1c-29c7-5fc5-9eae-4512b626a3d7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "How do you find the perimeter of a square?" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b7642cc-29be-5f1a-9a16-ef318c444413" :answer/id #uuid "6b7642cc-29be-5f1a-9a16-ef318c444413" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Sum of the measures of the angles in a pentagon." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b67f3de7-0824-5db8-a89a-109dbb1c1bc7" :answer/id #uuid "b67f3de7-0824-5db8-a89a-109dbb1c1bc7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The diameter of a circle." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a6a5fdc-fdac-5d72-9181-7f0590bf65a9" :answer/id #uuid "2a6a5fdc-fdac-5d72-9181-7f0590bf65a9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The sides of a triangle." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c043e0c4-50de-5146-885c-1db3a041b406" :question/id #uuid "c043e0c4-50de-5146-885c-1db3a041b406" :question/math-academy-id "q-86474" :question/problem "Which of the following is a mathematical statement?" :question/worked-solution "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false. \n\nOf the given sentences, the only sentence that is either true or false is \"$3$ is a positive number.\" (This sentence is true.)\n\nAll the other sentences are neither true nor false." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-380bc244-a440-547b-ba59-6ef9a824239a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-380bc244-a440-547b-ba59-6ef9a824239a" :answer-field/id #uuid "380bc244-a440-547b-ba59-6ef9a824239a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-49e9a260-0e94-5cb3-af9e-5bd6c76591c6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-49e9a260-0e94-5cb3-af9e-5bd6c76591c6" "answer-d8d95ecb-8d5b-5513-a75e-df53d3116d9c" "answer-a6623cc7-d894-575f-ac65-b336274a6064" "answer-3409f4e0-8718-5b95-bbe2-22462e3350dc" "answer-8a0bcc08-59f5-51f5-98d4-9305b9e19887"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49e9a260-0e94-5cb3-af9e-5bd6c76591c6" :answer/id #uuid "49e9a260-0e94-5cb3-af9e-5bd6c76591c6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3$ is a positive number." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d8d95ecb-8d5b-5513-a75e-df53d3116d9c" :answer/id #uuid "d8d95ecb-8d5b-5513-a75e-df53d3116d9c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The hypotenuse of a triangle." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6623cc7-d894-575f-ac65-b336274a6064" :answer/id #uuid "a6623cc7-d894-575f-ac65-b336274a6064" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The number $\\pi .$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3409f4e0-8718-5b95-bbe2-22462e3350dc" :answer/id #uuid "3409f4e0-8718-5b95-bbe2-22462e3350dc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The set of the odd numbers." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a0bcc08-59f5-51f5-98d4-9305b9e19887" :answer/id #uuid "8a0bcc08-59f5-51f5-98d4-9305b9e19887" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Why is $2$ an even number?" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0a9725fe-5d32-5217-81b5-21b1fce3c258" :question/id #uuid "0a9725fe-5d32-5217-81b5-21b1fce3c258" :question/math-academy-id "q-174417" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical statements?\n\n- $P:5\\,|\\,9$\n\n- $Q:\\sqrt{2}+0.2$\n\n- $R:\\sqrt{2}\\in R$" :question/worked-solution "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options: \n\n- $P$ is a statement. This statement is *false* because $5$ does not divide $9.$\n\n- $Q$ is *not* a statement because it is neither true nor false.\n\n- $R$ is a statement. This statement is *true* because $\\sqrt{2}$ is a real number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P$ and $R$ only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e60f71c4-9ac3-5f6b-9e7c-eca1c14c1978"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e60f71c4-9ac3-5f6b-9e7c-eca1c14c1978" :answer-field/id #uuid "e60f71c4-9ac3-5f6b-9e7c-eca1c14c1978" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d1069563-eea1-5f35-b63b-584fe5edde86" :answer-field/choices ["answer-73f80b23-1966-55fe-99ec-3a0c34dff20d" "answer-d1069563-eea1-5f35-b63b-584fe5edde86" "answer-b9bd5ee1-380b-5707-9141-9827a7e72d0b" "answer-4ea61359-4851-516b-b2a3-c6c648515cbf" "answer-c93f27ca-d6ca-5413-98d4-27b595552a02"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-73f80b23-1966-55fe-99ec-3a0c34dff20d" :answer/id #uuid "73f80b23-1966-55fe-99ec-3a0c34dff20d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P$  only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d1069563-eea1-5f35-b63b-584fe5edde86" :answer/id #uuid "d1069563-eea1-5f35-b63b-584fe5edde86" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P$ and $R$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b9bd5ee1-380b-5707-9141-9827a7e72d0b" :answer/id #uuid "b9bd5ee1-380b-5707-9141-9827a7e72d0b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q$ and $R$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ea61359-4851-516b-b2a3-c6c648515cbf" :answer/id #uuid "4ea61359-4851-516b-b2a3-c6c648515cbf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c93f27ca-d6ca-5413-98d4-27b595552a02" :answer/id #uuid "c93f27ca-d6ca-5413-98d4-27b595552a02" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$R$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4681538e-2de2-56f3-881c-562aebb342a4" :question/id #uuid "4681538e-2de2-56f3-881c-562aebb342a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-174421" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical statements?\n\n- $P:\\{2,3,7\\}\\cap \\{3,5,6\\}=∅$\n\n- $Q:{\\pi }^{2}-\\pi $\n\n- $R:3$ is a prime number." :question/worked-solution "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options: \n\n- $P$ is a statement. This statement is *false* because the intersection of the given sets is the set $\\{3\\}.$\n\n- $Q$ is *not* a statement because it is neither true nor false.\n\n- $R$ is a statement. This statement is *true* since $3$ is indeed a prime number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P$ and $R$ only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9bc23c46-3bd3-5315-a27d-9984de9363ff"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9bc23c46-3bd3-5315-a27d-9984de9363ff" :answer-field/id #uuid "9bc23c46-3bd3-5315-a27d-9984de9363ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-716d255d-da8a-543a-b7e5-474422b51ccf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7fa33b89-066a-5994-a5c6-4b947c94af99" "answer-716d255d-da8a-543a-b7e5-474422b51ccf" "answer-e22cde76-a74c-500b-b6af-756ccafc7a0f" "answer-c7d3dadc-f62a-5cdf-b969-e5976107e24e" "answer-241ec206-34ba-5db3-8740-a7379250c1e3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7fa33b89-066a-5994-a5c6-4b947c94af99" :answer/id #uuid "7fa33b89-066a-5994-a5c6-4b947c94af99" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P$ and $Q$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-716d255d-da8a-543a-b7e5-474422b51ccf" :answer/id #uuid "716d255d-da8a-543a-b7e5-474422b51ccf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P$ and $R$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e22cde76-a74c-500b-b6af-756ccafc7a0f" :answer/id #uuid "e22cde76-a74c-500b-b6af-756ccafc7a0f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7d3dadc-f62a-5cdf-b969-e5976107e24e" :answer/id #uuid "c7d3dadc-f62a-5cdf-b969-e5976107e24e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q$ and $R$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-241ec206-34ba-5db3-8740-a7379250c1e3" :answer/id #uuid "241ec206-34ba-5db3-8740-a7379250c1e3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3bd80b9b-2655-5bf4-bdf9-f7428c6e7e13" :question/id #uuid "3bd80b9b-2655-5bf4-bdf9-f7428c6e7e13" :question/math-academy-id "q-175327" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical predicates of one variable?\n\nI. $z$ divided by $10.$\n\nII. $x\\times 3$\n\nIII. $y+3$ is an odd number." :question/worked-solution "A *predicate* of one variable is a sentence that contains the variable defined on some *universal set* and has the property that when we substitute any concrete value of the variable into the predicate, the result becomes a statement that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our options. \n\n- Option I is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $z$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option II is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $x$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option III is a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $y$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-99fd9b59-7583-550f-9b77-a9aef65a8d04"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-99fd9b59-7583-550f-9b77-a9aef65a8d04" :answer-field/id #uuid "99fd9b59-7583-550f-9b77-a9aef65a8d04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-dafd16df-e541-559b-bbe3-f28f607b45b9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-01804a80-5ad0-5362-964c-9ececb6d064d" "answer-3b8e51e4-40fa-57ba-90ff-180ebb919ccb" "answer-8405f8f8-e192-530e-9104-fc411cda42f6" "answer-725de94a-3ee8-5f32-b2e7-5e74ed4217f0" "answer-dafd16df-e541-559b-bbe3-f28f607b45b9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01804a80-5ad0-5362-964c-9ececb6d064d" :answer/id #uuid "01804a80-5ad0-5362-964c-9ececb6d064d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b8e51e4-40fa-57ba-90ff-180ebb919ccb" :answer/id #uuid "3b8e51e4-40fa-57ba-90ff-180ebb919ccb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8405f8f8-e192-530e-9104-fc411cda42f6" :answer/id #uuid "8405f8f8-e192-530e-9104-fc411cda42f6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-725de94a-3ee8-5f32-b2e7-5e74ed4217f0" :answer/id #uuid "725de94a-3ee8-5f32-b2e7-5e74ed4217f0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dafd16df-e541-559b-bbe3-f28f607b45b9" :answer/id #uuid "dafd16df-e541-559b-bbe3-f28f607b45b9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f4fa3c45-5e91-57f0-a165-1adda22fdfd5" :question/id #uuid "f4fa3c45-5e91-57f0-a165-1adda22fdfd5" :question/math-academy-id "q-175340" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical predicates of one variable?\n\nI. $P(n):$ ${n}^{2}$ is odd.\n\nII. $Q(x):$ $(x+2)|5$\n\nIII. $R(y):$ $y$ is a multiple of $4.$" :question/worked-solution "A *predicate* of one variable is a sentence that contains the variable defined on some *universal set* and has the property that when we substitute any concrete value of the variable into the predicate, the result becomes a statement that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our options. \n\n- Option I is a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $n$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option II is a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $x$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option III is a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $y$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dd1c7fcd-33d6-50f3-a903-c3e604c9e00d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dd1c7fcd-33d6-50f3-a903-c3e604c9e00d" :answer-field/id #uuid "dd1c7fcd-33d6-50f3-a903-c3e604c9e00d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e0274858-530a-5336-a244-3ab577098764" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ce19c34c-55f0-53bd-90d0-5654a556e400" "answer-3df4871b-4533-56fb-bc7b-dd5a4905e0bc" "answer-e0274858-530a-5336-a244-3ab577098764" "answer-baae5ccd-bb5f-5df3-b5b6-228fe5505245" "answer-d12f7ee4-e6d2-572c-bc6f-c2a4f216d210"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce19c34c-55f0-53bd-90d0-5654a556e400" :answer/id #uuid "ce19c34c-55f0-53bd-90d0-5654a556e400" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3df4871b-4533-56fb-bc7b-dd5a4905e0bc" :answer/id #uuid "3df4871b-4533-56fb-bc7b-dd5a4905e0bc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e0274858-530a-5336-a244-3ab577098764" :answer/id #uuid "e0274858-530a-5336-a244-3ab577098764" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-baae5ccd-bb5f-5df3-b5b6-228fe5505245" :answer/id #uuid "baae5ccd-bb5f-5df3-b5b6-228fe5505245" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d12f7ee4-e6d2-572c-bc6f-c2a4f216d210" :answer/id #uuid "d12f7ee4-e6d2-572c-bc6f-c2a4f216d210" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186056004 :tutorial/content "A **mathematical statement** is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either **true** or **false**.\n\nFor example:\n\n- The sentence, \"The sum of $1$ and $2$ is $3$\" is a mathematical statement because it is *true.*\n\n- Likewise, \"$2+2=5$\" is a mathematical statement because it is *false.*\n\nThe following examples are *not* mathematical statements:\n\n- \"Find the sum of $1$ and $2$\" is *not* a mathematical statement because it is neither true nor false. It is an instruction.\n\n- \"What is the sum of $1$ and $2?$\" is *not* a mathematical statement because it is neither true nor false. It is a question.\n\n- Similarly, \"$6+9$\" is *not* a mathematical statement because it is neither true nor false.\n\nWe often use upper-case letters such as $P, Q,$ and $R$ to represent statements. For example:\n\n- $P:$ The sum of two even integers is odd.\n\n- $Q: 3 \\in \\mathbb Z$\n\n- $R: \\{2,4,6\\ldots\\}\\cup \\{1,3,5,\\ldots\\} = \\mathbb N$\n\nIn this case, the statements $Q$ and $R$ are true, whereas statement $P$ is false." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186056051 :tutorial/content "A **predicate** (or **open sentence**) of one variable is a sentence that contains a variable defined on some *universal set* and has the property that when we substitute a concrete value of the variable into the predicate, the result becomes a mathematical statement that is either *true* or *false*.\n\nFor example, consider the following predicate:\n\n$x > 1$\n\nThis is a predicate because substituting concrete values for $x$ gives a mathematical statement.\n\nFor instance: \n\n- Substituting $x=2$ gives the *true* statement \"$2 > 1$\"\n\n- Substituting $x=5$ gives the *true* statement \"$5 > 1$\"\n\n- Substituting $x=0$ gives the *false* statement \"$0 > 1$\"\n\nWe denote predicates using capital letters and the corresponding variable in parentheses. In this example, we can write our predicate more formally as follows:\n\n$P(x):$ $x > 1$\n\nAny predicate must be defined with its **universal set,** which is the set from which we are allowed to pull the concrete values of the variable. So, we could state our predicate more formally as\n\n$P(x):$ $x > 1,$ $\\quad$ where $x \\in \\mathbb{R}.$\n\nThe universal set can often be identified from the context and doesn't need to be explicitly stated. For example, if we have the predicate \n\n$n$ is divisible by 5,\n\nwe can assume that $n$ is defined on the set of all integers, i.e., $n \\in \\mathbb{Z}.$\n\nIn math, *any equation or inequality is a predicate*. However, a sentence containing a variable is not necessarily a predicate. For example, the sentence \n\n$\\qquad$ \"What is the sign of $y?$\"\n\nis *not* a predicate because substituting a concrete value for $y$ does not give a mathematical statement. Instead, it gives a question. \n\nSimilarly, \n\n$z^2-5$\n\nis *not* a predicate either. It's just an expression." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054913 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184197 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ffe00adb-b1a9-53a2-98b2-87735ab0e412" "question-c14fd620-27ea-593f-816e-9c2134638c65"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ffe00adb-b1a9-53a2-98b2-87735ab0e412" :question/id #uuid "ffe00adb-b1a9-53a2-98b2-87735ab0e412" :question/math-academy-id "q-95279" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]$ has two negative singular values.\n\nII. Any $4\\times 5$ matrix $A$ has at most $5$ distinct singular values.\n\nIII. Any $8\\times 4$ matrix $A$ has at most $8$ distinct singular values." :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false.  All singular values of any matrix are non-negative. So, \n$A$  can't have any negative singular value.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, since $A$ is a $4\\times 5$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $5\\times 4$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $5\\times 5$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{5\\times 4}\\times {A}_{4\\times 5}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{5\\times 5}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $5$ distinct singular values.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is a $8\\times 4$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $4\\times 8$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $4\\times 4$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{4\\times 8}\\times {A}_{8\\times 4}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{4\\times 4}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $4$ distinct singular values.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0ff2e77b-8d7a-52d3-9995-01bf83f68824"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0ff2e77b-8d7a-52d3-9995-01bf83f68824" :answer-field/id #uuid "0ff2e77b-8d7a-52d3-9995-01bf83f68824" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2884dfb8-f94e-5c91-ad86-e9f24321844f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d14824a1-5da1-565c-9821-2d89beac20eb" "answer-6d73a7ca-949e-5940-a71c-8360af1c5dd7" "answer-357cad34-4bc7-513b-b925-b09513a89749" "answer-2884dfb8-f94e-5c91-ad86-e9f24321844f" "answer-a72b1823-445c-5fca-a1a8-59da7d424147"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d14824a1-5da1-565c-9821-2d89beac20eb" :answer/id #uuid "d14824a1-5da1-565c-9821-2d89beac20eb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d73a7ca-949e-5940-a71c-8360af1c5dd7" :answer/id #uuid "6d73a7ca-949e-5940-a71c-8360af1c5dd7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-357cad34-4bc7-513b-b925-b09513a89749" :answer/id #uuid "357cad34-4bc7-513b-b925-b09513a89749" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2884dfb8-f94e-5c91-ad86-e9f24321844f" :answer/id #uuid "2884dfb8-f94e-5c91-ad86-e9f24321844f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a72b1823-445c-5fca-a1a8-59da7d424147" :answer/id #uuid "a72b1823-445c-5fca-a1a8-59da7d424147" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c14fd620-27ea-593f-816e-9c2134638c65" :question/id #uuid "c14fd620-27ea-593f-816e-9c2134638c65" :question/math-academy-id "q-139496" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. Any $5\\times 3$ matrix $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values.\n\nII. Any $3\\times 5$ matrix $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values.\n\nIII. The singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]$ are negative." :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $A$ is a $5\\times 3$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $3\\times 5$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $3\\times 3$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{3\\times 5}\\times {A}_{5\\times 3}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{3\\times 3}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values.\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $A$ is a $3\\times 5$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $5\\times 3$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $5\\times 5$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{5\\times 3}\\times {A}_{3\\times 5}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{5\\times 5}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $5$ distinct singular values.\n\n- Statement III is false. All singular values of any matrix are non-negative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-38f6bcff-7304-5d0b-a0af-efe2d713e856"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-38f6bcff-7304-5d0b-a0af-efe2d713e856" :answer-field/id #uuid "38f6bcff-7304-5d0b-a0af-efe2d713e856" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-faf2a892-5d88-5731-80fa-930f46707b27" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ce9dcab1-550f-5fde-9320-31c024c5bc69" "answer-705cd4e5-6f0f-570c-82b2-98b917b98f02" "answer-faf2a892-5d88-5731-80fa-930f46707b27" "answer-4ae6732b-eca3-5cb4-9976-d76d9aaaaa62" "answer-349f736d-de0d-599c-94b3-d79307c82b40"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce9dcab1-550f-5fde-9320-31c024c5bc69" :answer/id #uuid "ce9dcab1-550f-5fde-9320-31c024c5bc69" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-705cd4e5-6f0f-570c-82b2-98b917b98f02" :answer/id #uuid "705cd4e5-6f0f-570c-82b2-98b917b98f02" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-faf2a892-5d88-5731-80fa-930f46707b27" :answer/id #uuid "faf2a892-5d88-5731-80fa-930f46707b27" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ae6732b-eca3-5cb4-9976-d76d9aaaaa62" :answer/id #uuid "4ae6732b-eca3-5cb4-9976-d76d9aaaaa62" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-349f736d-de0d-599c-94b3-d79307c82b40" :answer/id #uuid "349f736d-de0d-599c-94b3-d79307c82b40" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-456c2843-f8fd-5ae4-a5f7-4b0d67446bb6" :activity/id #uuid "456c2843-f8fd-5ae4-a5f7-4b0d67446bb6" :activity/title "Computing the Singular Values of a Matrix" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049462 :activity/course 17592186046669 :activity/steps ["step-b2c6bcad-aab2-51b4-8844-1a9ba59e06d8" "step-d45aa491-e815-5760-826e-8fe2c46d302f" "step-92011cee-25ec-5645-8649-3c5082cdb2df" "step-c7261c21-321e-5abd-8187-70f19af061de" "step-d141f860-642e-5d1b-b75f-8196aeaa74cc"] :activity/first-step "step-b2c6bcad-aab2-51b4-8844-1a9ba59e06d8" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-b2c6bcad-aab2-51b4-8844-1a9ba59e06d8" :step/id #uuid "b2c6bcad-aab2-51b4-8844-1a9ba59e06d8" :step/content 17592186543482 :step/next "step-d45aa491-e815-5760-826e-8fe2c46d302f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-d45aa491-e815-5760-826e-8fe2c46d302f" :step/id #uuid "d45aa491-e815-5760-826e-8fe2c46d302f" :step/content "question-ffe00adb-b1a9-53a2-98b2-87735ab0e412" :step/next "step-92011cee-25ec-5645-8649-3c5082cdb2df" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-92011cee-25ec-5645-8649-3c5082cdb2df" :step/id #uuid "92011cee-25ec-5645-8649-3c5082cdb2df" :step/content 17592186404794 :step/next "step-c7261c21-321e-5abd-8187-70f19af061de" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c7261c21-321e-5abd-8187-70f19af061de" :step/id #uuid "c7261c21-321e-5abd-8187-70f19af061de" :step/content 17592186415578 :step/next "step-d141f860-642e-5d1b-b75f-8196aeaa74cc" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-d141f860-642e-5d1b-b75f-8196aeaa74cc" :step/id #uuid "d141f860-642e-5d1b-b75f-8196aeaa74cc" :step/content "question-c14fd620-27ea-593f-816e-9c2134638c65" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186100839 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-bae7b49c-3856-514a-a9ab-b99ea914cf24" "question-3b6389e0-fab8-5e1d-bb5a-1e8d075edcaa"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-bae7b49c-3856-514a-a9ab-b99ea914cf24" :question/id #uuid "bae7b49c-3856-514a-a9ab-b99ea914cf24" :question/math-academy-id "q-117054" :question/problem "![](images/2c/2cfba1072b37cd316349997201ada6e67af702926214abec22a1ef5ae6543c5a.png)\n\nConsider a box with a square base with side lengths $x$ and height $y,$ as shown above. The volume of the box is $125$ cubic units. Given that the surface area of the box has been minimized, find the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1**: We need to find the value of $x$ such that the surface area\n\n$$\nS=2{x}^{2}+4xy\n$$\n\nis the smallest possible value.\n\n**Step 2**: The volume is exactly $125$ cubic units. So, we have the constraint equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =x\\cdot x\\cdot y \\\\ 125 & ={x}^{2}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We make $y$ the subject of the constraint equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}y & =125 \\\\ y & =\\frac{125}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute the above into our expression for $S,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2{x}^{2}+4xy \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}+4x\\cdot \\frac{125}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}+\\frac{500}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: We solve the equation ${S}^{′}(x)=0.$ Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n{S}^{′}(x)=4x-\\frac{500}{{x}^{2}},\n$$\n\nand solving for the stationary points, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}^{′}(x) & =0 \\\\ 4x-\\frac{500}{{x}^{2}} & =0 \\\\ 4x & =\\frac{500}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ 4{x}^{3} & =500 \\\\ {x}^{3} & =125 \\\\ x & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 5**: We confirm that $x=5$ is a minimum using the second derivative test. The second derivative is\n\n$$\n{S}^{″}(x)=4+\\frac{1\\,000}{{x}^{3}}\\,⟹\\,{S}^{″}(5)=4+8=12>0.\n$$\n\nSince ${S}^{″}(5)$ is positive, we conclude that $x=5$ is indeed a minimum of $S(x).$\n\nTherefore, the box with the smallest possible surface area has side length $x=5$ units." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-907188cd-1b8a-5efd-a8a3-c00dedfb9afa"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-907188cd-1b8a-5efd-a8a3-c00dedfb9afa" :answer-field/id #uuid "907188cd-1b8a-5efd-a8a3-c00dedfb9afa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-534e43c0-1360-5b0d-8a4a-5d2bde094e21" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3fbea327-41aa-5fdc-a977-23866bec8887" "answer-f0dc00a2-c124-5ff2-b78f-80d14094484c" "answer-f4a02da5-372b-5869-879e-c7b98972e685" "answer-f00913c9-54b0-51ef-a4b0-ef296a0170c9" "answer-534e43c0-1360-5b0d-8a4a-5d2bde094e21"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3fbea327-41aa-5fdc-a977-23866bec8887" :answer/id #uuid "3fbea327-41aa-5fdc-a977-23866bec8887" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$10$ units" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f0dc00a2-c124-5ff2-b78f-80d14094484c" :answer/id #uuid "f0dc00a2-c124-5ff2-b78f-80d14094484c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$15$ units" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4a02da5-372b-5869-879e-c7b98972e685" :answer/id #uuid "f4a02da5-372b-5869-879e-c7b98972e685" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$ units" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f00913c9-54b0-51ef-a4b0-ef296a0170c9" :answer/id #uuid "f00913c9-54b0-51ef-a4b0-ef296a0170c9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4$ units" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-534e43c0-1360-5b0d-8a4a-5d2bde094e21" :answer/id #uuid "534e43c0-1360-5b0d-8a4a-5d2bde094e21" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$5$ units" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186100940 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8973c685-fd2c-51e0-89ff-171e4339d4cb" "question-88d64cef-5be0-59d0-8f76-951d4350e51b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8973c685-fd2c-51e0-89ff-171e4339d4cb" :question/id #uuid "8973c685-fd2c-51e0-89ff-171e4339d4cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-117217" :question/problem "![](images/af/afc68dbb5c336cff31e75f5ed92dd853c8fc7ec43e8fa66539d27d83b9e2070f.png)\n\nA box with no lid and a square base has a manufacturing cost that depends on two materials. The material for the base costs $$3$ per square meter, and the material for the lateral faces costs $$5$ per square meter. The box must have a volume of $2\\,{m}^{3}.$\n\nWhat is the value of $x$ for the box that has the smallest production cost?" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1**: We need to find the value of $x$ such that the manufacturing cost\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =3{x}^{2}+5\\cdot 4xy \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}+20xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis the smallest possible value.\n\n**Step 2**: The volume must be $2\\,{m}^{3}.$ So, we have the constraint equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =x\\cdot x\\cdot y \\\\ 2 & ={x}^{2}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We make $y$ the subject of the constraint equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}y & =2 \\\\ y & =\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute the above into our expression for $C,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =3{x}^{2}+20xy \\\\ C & =3{x}^{2}+20x\\cdot \\frac{2}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ C & =3{x}^{2}+\\frac{40}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: We solve the equation ${C}^{′}(x)=0.$ Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n{C}^{′}(x)=6x-\\frac{40}{{x}^{2}},\n$$\n\nand solving for the stationary points, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{′}(x) & =0 \\\\ 6x-\\frac{40}{{x}^{2}} & =0 \\\\ 6{x}^{3} & =40 \\\\ {x}^{3} & =\\frac{20}{3} \\\\ x & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{20}{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 5**: We confirm that $x=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{20}{3}}$ is a minimum using the second derivative test. The second derivative is\n\n$$\n{C}^{″}(x)=6+\\frac{80}{{x}^{3}}\\,⟹\\,{C}^{″}(\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{20}{3}})=6+12=18>0.\n$$\n\nSince ${C}^{″}(\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{20}{3}})$ is positive, we conclude that $x=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{20}{3}}$ is indeed a minimum of $C(x).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-76985055-fc94-55ff-998a-6e253b938977"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-76985055-fc94-55ff-998a-6e253b938977" :answer-field/id #uuid "76985055-fc94-55ff-998a-6e253b938977" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-72638d95-8910-5c23-aa5c-c06b64acc003" :answer-field/choices ["answer-02932fbd-ee3d-58bf-9d40-e6c4b5772ce5" "answer-2c37baac-a6d7-52ff-b039-36b9f3d4538b" "answer-0653430e-b3f6-5da7-8b4a-42f0139025c0" "answer-13d2aacc-5287-5151-8fa4-4b990a54d3bd" "answer-72638d95-8910-5c23-aa5c-c06b64acc003"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-02932fbd-ee3d-58bf-9d40-e6c4b5772ce5" :answer/id #uuid "02932fbd-ee3d-58bf-9d40-e6c4b5772ce5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18\\,m" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c37baac-a6d7-52ff-b039-36b9f3d4538b" :answer/id #uuid "2c37baac-a6d7-52ff-b039-36b9f3d4538b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{5}{3}}\\,m" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0653430e-b3f6-5da7-8b4a-42f0139025c0" :answer/id #uuid "0653430e-b3f6-5da7-8b4a-42f0139025c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{20}{3}\\,m" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-13d2aacc-5287-5151-8fa4-4b990a54d3bd" :answer/id #uuid "13d2aacc-5287-5151-8fa4-4b990a54d3bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{7}\\,m" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-72638d95-8910-5c23-aa5c-c06b64acc003" :answer/id #uuid "72638d95-8910-5c23-aa5c-c06b64acc003" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{20}{3}}\\,m" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3b6389e0-fab8-5e1d-bb5a-1e8d075edcaa" :question/id #uuid "3b6389e0-fab8-5e1d-bb5a-1e8d075edcaa" :question/math-academy-id "q-346784" :question/problem "![](images/4c/4cafc2891cfd957aad10e876d51757e8c6d7e84844927cb57ce1c2e704fe5b55.png)\n\nConsider a box with width $x,$ height $y,$ and depth $z,$ as shown above. The depth of the box is three times its width. Given that the box's volume is $972$ cubic units, what is the smallest possible surface area ${S}_{\\text{min}}$ of the box? Do not round the answer.\n\n${S}_{\\text{min}}=$\n{{field-1}} square units" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1**: We need to find the value of $x$ such that the surface area\n\n$$\nS=2xz+2xy+2yz\n$$\n\nis the smallest possible value.\n\n**Step 2**: The volume is $972$ cubic units. So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =x\\cdot y\\cdot z \\\\ 972 & =xyz.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the fact that $z=3x,$ we get the constraint equation\n\n$$\n972=3{x}^{2}y.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We make $y$ the subject of the constraint equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}y & =972 \\\\ y & =\\frac{324}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute the above into our expression for $S,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2xz+2xy+2yz \\\\  & =2x(3x)+2x(\\frac{324}{{x}^{2}})+2(\\frac{324}{{x}^{2}})(3x) \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}+\\frac{648}{x}+\\frac{1944}{x} \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}+\\frac{2592}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: We solve the equation ${S}^{′}(x)=0.$ Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n{S}^{′}(x)=12x-\\frac{2592}{{x}^{2}},\n$$\n\nand solving for the stationary points, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}^{′}(x) & =0 \\\\ 12x-\\frac{2592}{{x}^{2}} & =0 \\\\ 12{x}^{3}-2592 & =0 \\\\ 12{x}^{3} & =2592 \\\\ {x}^{3} & =216 \\\\ x & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 5**: We confirm that $x=6$ is a minimum using the second derivative test. The second derivative is\n\n$$\n{S}^{″}(x)=12+\\frac{5184}{{x}^{3}}\\,⟹\\,{S}^{″}(6)=12+24=36>0.\n$$\n\nSince ${S}^{″}(6)$ is positive, we conclude that $x=6$ is indeed a minimum.\n\nNow, the smallest surface area ${S}_{\\text{min}}$ that the box can have is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{\\text{min}}=S(6) & =6(6)^{2}+\\frac{2592}{6} \\\\  & =648\\,\\text{square units}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-29d8dbeb-a278-5ecd-a7ab-cdc1d19cdc10"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-29d8dbeb-a278-5ecd-a7ab-cdc1d19cdc10" :answer-field/id #uuid "29d8dbeb-a278-5ecd-a7ab-cdc1d19cdc10" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-b3088ae4-d68a-57e8-b0d8-0c5b606e66de" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b3088ae4-d68a-57e8-b0d8-0c5b606e66de"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b3088ae4-d68a-57e8-b0d8-0c5b606e66de" :answer/id #uuid "b3088ae4-d68a-57e8-b0d8-0c5b606e66de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "648" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-88d64cef-5be0-59d0-8f76-951d4350e51b" :question/id #uuid "88d64cef-5be0-59d0-8f76-951d4350e51b" :question/math-academy-id "q-347083" :question/problem "![](images/d6/d67ba70d92807f0a7298fb8222252a047f7eec03a26878a5aa95b0fb82a7335c.png)\n\nA box with no lid whose depth $z$ is $3$ times its height $y$ has a manufacturing cost that depends on two materials. The material for the base costs $$2$ per square meter, and the material for the lateral faces costs $$1$ per square meter. The box must have a volume of $972\\,{m}^{3}.$\n\nWhat is the value of $z$ for the box that has the smallest production cost? Do not round the answer.\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}} units" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1**: We need to find the value of $z$ such that the manufacturing cost\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =2xz+1\\cdot 2xy+1\\cdot 2yz \\\\  & =2xz+2xy+2yz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis the smallest possible value.\n\n**Step 2**: The volume must be $972\\,{m}^{3}.$ So, we have the constraint equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =x\\cdot z\\cdot y \\\\ 972 & =x\\cdot z\\cdot (\\frac{z}{3}) \\\\ 972 & =\\frac{1}{3}x{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We make $x$ the subject of the constraint equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}x{z}^{2} & =972 \\\\ x & =\\frac{2916}{{z}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute the above into our expression for $C,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =2xz+2xy+2yz \\\\  & =2\\,(\\frac{2916}{{z}^{2}})\\,z+2\\,(\\frac{2916}{{z}^{2}})\\,(\\frac{z}{3})+2\\,(\\frac{z}{3})\\,z \\\\  & =\\frac{5832}{z}+\\frac{1944}{z}+\\frac{2}{3}{z}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7776}{z}+\\frac{2}{3}{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: We solve the equation ${C}^{′}(z)=0.$ Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n{C}^{′}(z)=\\frac{4}{3}z-\\frac{7776}{{z}^{2}},\n$$\n\nand solving for the stationary points, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{′}(z) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}z-\\frac{7776}{{z}^{2}} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}{z}^{3} & =7776 \\\\ {z}^{3} & =5832 \\\\ z & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 5**: We confirm that $z=18$ is a minimum using the second derivative test. The second derivative is\n\n$$\n{C}^{″}(z)=\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{15552}{{z}^{3}}\\,⟹\\,{C}^{″}(18)=\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{8}{3}=4>0.\n$$\n\nSince ${C}^{″}(18)$ is positive, we conclude that $z=18$ is indeed a minimum of $C(z).$\n\nTherefore, the production cost is the smallest when $z=18$ units." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2ae05d3c-21d9-5363-8872-60ad0b3f9a59"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2ae05d3c-21d9-5363-8872-60ad0b3f9a59" :answer-field/id #uuid "2ae05d3c-21d9-5363-8872-60ad0b3f9a59" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-26d46271-3014-5476-b936-8ff5de06d051" :answer-field/choices ["answer-26d46271-3014-5476-b936-8ff5de06d051"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26d46271-3014-5476-b936-8ff5de06d051" :answer/id #uuid "26d46271-3014-5476-b936-8ff5de06d051" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186100939 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-35d621eb-cf33-51a5-9f2c-6f01d51e0a4e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-35d621eb-cf33-51a5-9f2c-6f01d51e0a4e" :question/id #uuid "35d621eb-cf33-51a5-9f2c-6f01d51e0a4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-347273" :question/problem "![](images/12/12a9961800e0578de92b428e1a1a6ba5e10e25fe635a90f85c772f9bf73dc997.png)\n\nA piece of cardboard measures $15\\,cm\\times 7\\,cm.$ A tray of height $y\\,\\text{cm}$ is formed by cutting a $y\\times y\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}$ square from each of the corners and folding up the sides, as shown in the diagram. Determine the height $y$ of the box that gives the maximum possible volume.\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}} $\\text{cm}$" :question/worked-solution "**Step 1**: We need to find the values of $x,y,$ and $z$ such that the volume\n\n$$\nV=xyz\n$$\n\nis the greatest possible value.\n\n**Step 2**: Notice that the width $x$ and the depth $z$ of the tray are given by\n\n$$\nx=15-2y,\\,z=7-2y.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $x>0$ and $z>0,$ we must have that $15-2y>0$ and $7-2y>0$, hence $y<\\frac{7}{2}.$ Therefore, the range of validity for $y$ is $0<y<\\frac{7}{2}.$\n\n**Step 3**: Substituting the above into the expression for $V,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =xyz \\\\  & =(15-2y)(y)(7-2y) \\\\  & =4{y}^{3}-44{y}^{2}+105y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: We solve the equation ${V}^{′}(y)=0.$ Taking the first derivative, we have\n\n$$\n{V}^{′}(y)=12{y}^{2}-88y+105,\n$$\n\nand solving for the stationary points, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}^{′}(y) & =0 \\\\ 12{y}^{2}-88y+105 & =0 \\\\ y & =\\frac{3}{2},\\,\\frac{35}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe discard $\\frac{35}{6}$ since we already know that $0<y<\\frac{7}{2}.$\n\n**Step 5**: We confirm that $\\frac{3}{2}$ is a maximum using the second derivative test. The second derivative is\n\n$$\n{V}^{″}(y)=24y-88.\n$$\n\nSince ${V}^{″}(\\frac{3}{2})$ is negative, we conclude that $\\frac{3}{2}$ is indeed a maximum of $V(y).$\n\nTherefore, the height of the box with the maximum volume is $y=\\frac{3}{2}\\text{ cm}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-41fc7962-a273-588e-89ef-1ba97b8bff24"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-41fc7962-a273-588e-89ef-1ba97b8bff24" :answer-field/id #uuid "41fc7962-a273-588e-89ef-1ba97b8bff24" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-fd9f3f04-dec2-59a4-90c7-4e80640a9ce0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fd9f3f04-dec2-59a4-90c7-4e80640a9ce0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd9f3f04-dec2-59a4-90c7-4e80640a9ce0" :answer/id #uuid "fd9f3f04-dec2-59a4-90c7-4e80640a9ce0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-d39c546e-aa9b-57f9-9da7-aa0899e1ca37" :activity/id #uuid "d39c546e-aa9b-57f9-9da7-aa0899e1ca37" :activity/title "Optimization Problems Involving Boxes and Trays" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050100 :activity/course 17592186046669 :activity/steps ["step-2470c84c-c97b-513d-8e62-311c5ead05dc" "step-986d328c-4039-5272-94a8-a5b54b4004c1" "step-afee5c19-21de-5dac-b2a9-ef66458e0dec" "step-83c4667d-a7a5-57bc-aaae-222f06c3f1de" "step-3